WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
This diagram models the progression to
achieve institutional maturity.

2
00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.500
First is understanding foundational
principles.

3
00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:09.340
Investigators then apply these practices
to workflows.

4
00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:12.600
Next, researchers solve complex ethical
dilemmas.

5
00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:16.980
At the advocacy threshold, they promote
responsible practices.

6
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:21.300
Finally, they foster a system addressing
structural barriers.

7
00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:25.680
Ethical compliance requires a continuous
progression toward institutional

8
00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:30.700
resilience. This chart models that
institutional assent through the integrity

9
00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:35.520
equation. The first variable tracks the
individual investigator's internal

10
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:39.820
attitude and cognitive habits. Because
individual judgment can be

11
00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:43.900
inconsistent, it is reinforced by external
frameworks and institutional

12
00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:48.260
standards. Combining consistent human
habit with these established rules

13
00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:52.160
produces the intended output—trustworthy
research.

14
00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:56.700
Here, trust in science is a systemic
byproduct of human habits functioning

15
00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:58.560
within external constraints.
